  "identity_and_authority": [
    "Actual Host-issued authenticated principal/native transport context is authoritative. Require current project authorization and principal/project workspace binding. No owner/root/trustedCaller boolean, executable path, argv, auth token or provider endpoint is accepted in a request.",
    "Resolve real workspace and current launch/security policy on the Host. Recheck before launch and on lease/permission change. A capability response or successful metadata probe is not a launch authorization.",
    "Use fixed native Codex executable/version/hash and Host-fixed permission/config arguments. No arbitrary caller command or dangerous bypass. Host-controlled working directory excludes project-local configuration; mandatory native platform policy remains authoritative.",
    "Use default_permissions plus the approved permissions profile; do not combine legacy --sandbox with it. workspace-read is the requested scope, not a proven OS/filesystem isolation claim until independently observed.",
    "Provider authentication remains CLI-owned. Never expose credentials, auth files, raw login output or Core scheduler/executor tokens to UI/CLI child environment."
  ],
  "capabilities_rules": [
    "can_submit is computed by Host policy for the requested bounded readonly task. Client cannot assert it. It does not imply execution/model/profile/cancel qualification.",
    "Installation/login metadata and verification are independent. Metadata success must not produce LIVE_OBSERVED or old Mu/model-qualified facts.",
    "readonly_turn/event_stream/cancel/task_history/request_lookup describe implemented operations; verification reports what was actually tested.",
    "token_delta is false in V1: ASSISTANT_MESSAGE is a whole observed message, not fabricated token streaming.",
    "write/resume/pause/per_tool_approval/file_diff/file_list/file_artifacts/attachments are false. UI disables those actions. Do not synthesize a V2 session_id to use old workspace.diff.",
    "can_submit=false must include reason_codes. Unsupported requested functionality is rejected rather than silently ignored.",
    "security_scope.hooks/mcp=PLATFORM_POLICY declares native platform ownership, not proof that extensions are disabled. Fixed flags request optional hooks/plugins disabled; mandatory platform policies are never bypassed. UI must keep verification states separate."
  ],
  "submit_and_recovery_rules": [
    "request_id is a stable mutation idempotency key, scoped to actual principal+project+operation. Store exact request hash and original response using existing idempotency storage in the same transaction as Task creation.",
    "Same key/same canonical payload returns the same Task and original response; same key/different payload is409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT. Replays never create another Task/Run or external launch.",
    "TaskRef is an immutable locator {project_id,task_id}, not a forged domain VersionRef. Task revision and RunRef are separately authoritative.",
    "After a transport timeout/UNKNOWN the renderer must not automatically resubmit or allocate a new request_id. Query GET tasks?project_id=...&request_id=original first.",
    "NOT_FOUND is a read observation, not proof the original request cannot still commit. Keep submission outcome UNKNOWN; allow read-only requery. An explicitly user-requested retry retains the exact original request_id and body.",
    "Run is created only by the sole Coordinator after Task commit. Harness task_type may be harness_turn; it does not require provider/model_config_ref or impersonate mu_turn.",
    "COMPLETED means reconciled native execution with an observed terminal protocol result, not independent business acceptance. No old Goal LIVE gate or formal result is upgraded."
  ],
  "cursor_rules": [
    "epoch, task_revision, sequence and every cursor are canonical decimal strings <=9223372036854775807. Cursor/sequence may be0 only where schema allows; epoch/revision/event sequence are positive. Never send JS numeric representations.",
    "Event sequence uses the existing project outbox monotonic sequence; versioned DTO projection is task-scoped. Do not reuse renderer timestamps or duplicate scheduler/event authority.",
    "Recent-task cursor and event cursor are different namespaces despite both being decimal strings; clients keep them separately and reset to0 when project/task changes.",
    "Event cursor is task-specific client state. Pages include only authorized events for the selected Task, with their actual nullable RunRef. next_cursor never moves backwards in an ordinary page.",
    "Persisted event_id/sequence are stable across replay. UI deduplicates and keeps the backend cursor; it does not acknowledge a later cursor before applying that page.",
    "A Run/epoch change does not reset the cursor. RUN_STARTED carries the new RunRef; preserve earlier events as history and use the authoritative current Task for cancel CAS. No automatic resume/relaunch is implied.",
    "Malformed/out-of-int64 cursor returns400 INVALID_REQUEST. A well-formed future/unavailable/pruned cursor returns200 with reset=true, events=[], snapshot=current Task, next_cursor=current authoritative task tail, has_more=false and end=Task.terminal.",
    "On reset the client replaces derived Task state with snapshot and discards its incremental event buffer; it never resubmits work. Poll from next_cursor only when end=false.",
    "For normal pages snapshot=null. end=true only when the Task is terminal AND this page has exhausted the persisted terminal event; a terminal Task with more event pages has end=false.",
    "When no events are returned and no reset is required, preserve cursor. has_more controls immediate next page; otherwise poll with backoff while end=false.",
    "Terminal Task state and its terminal event must commit atomically; do not report end merely from process exit or a non-authoritative cache."
  ],
  "cancel_rules": [
    "All CancelRequest fields are required. expected_run_id and expected_epoch must be either both null or both nonnull.",
    "Queued/pre-launch cancellation requires expected_run_id=null,expected_epoch=null and matching expected_task_revision. If Coordinator claimed meanwhile, return409 STATE_CONFLICT; do not cancel the newly observed Run automatically.",
    "Active cancellation requires exact expected_task_revision, expected_run_id and decimal expected_epoch against the actual current Run. Stale/foreign values return409 without affecting another Run.",
    "Cancel is idempotent under its own request_id and exact request hash. An already terminal matching target returns ALREADY_TERMINAL without launch/replay.",
    "CANCEL_REQUESTED acknowledges only durable intent. CANCELLED requires verified child/stream/cleanup terminal facts. Never claim rollback of external effects.",
    "The UI refreshes after STATE_CONFLICT and waits for another explicit user cancel action; it cannot silently substitute a new Run/epoch.",
    "UNKNOWN is not automatic retry or cancellation success. Later read-only reconciliation may refine status without relaunching."
  ],
  "event_payload_rules": {
    "TASK_QUEUED": "payload.task=current Task; payload.status=QUEUED; run=null.",
    "RUN_STARTED": "run=actual new RunRef; payload.status=STARTING or RUNNING.",
    "RUN_STATE": "payload.status=current observed lifecycle state.",
    "ASSISTANT_MESSAGE": "payload.text=one complete observed assistant message; no synthetic token deltas.",
    "TOOL_EVENT": "payload.tool=observed native tool id/name/phase/redacted summary; this is observation, not an approval bridge.",
    "LOG": "payload.text=bounded/redacted diagnostic; stderr is never parsed as a success protocol.",
    "TASK_TERMINAL": "payload.task=authoritative final Task; payload.status matches; payload.error mirrors failure if any.",
    "all": "All five payload keys exist; irrelevant keys are null. No raw secrets, executable argv, auth contents or unbounded tool transcripts are projected."
  },
  "task_status_rules": {
    "nonterminal": [
      "QUEUED",
      "STARTING",
      "RUNNING",
      "CANCEL_REQUESTED"
    ],
    "terminal": [
      "COMPLETED",
      "FAILED",
      "CANCELLED",
      "BLOCKED",
      "UNKNOWN"
    ],
    "note": "Terminal here means no automatic work/relaunch for this V1 request. UNKNOWN may later be refined by existing trusted reconciliation; V1 has no resume operation."
  },
  "http_errors": {
    "400": [
      "INVALID_REQUEST"
    ],
    "401": [
      "HOST_AUTH_REQUIRED"
    ],
    "403": [
      "FORBIDDEN",
      "WORKSPACE_REVOKED"
    ],
    "404": [
      "NOT_FOUND"
    ],
    "409": [
      "STATE_CONFLICT",
      "IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT",
      "HARNESS_AUTH_REQUIRED"
    ],
    "422": [
      "UNSUPPORTED_CAPABILITY"
    ],
    "500": [
      "INTERNAL_ERROR"
    ],
    "503": [
      "HARNESS_UNAVAILABLE"
    ],
    "execution_unknown": "Transport uncertainty is initially a client outcome; a persisted execution uncertainty is Task.status UNKNOWN/failure.code EXECUTION_UNKNOWN. Never encode uncertain launch as a fresh retry opportunity.",
    "retryable": "Advisory for read-only recovery only. Does not authorize automatic resubmission/cancel retry or a new request_id."
  },
  "transport_rules": [
    "Actual Host/native transport authenticates every route. Legacy V2/Mu routes remain compatible and unchanged.",
    "HTTP success response uses {api_version,data}; every failure uses {api_version,error}. No stack traces or raw CLI auth output.",
    "UI/Desktop bridge shares this exact interface. It supplies no authority booleans and preserves decimal strings end to end.",
    "Request prompt is bounded to65536 UTF8 bytes; no attachments in V1. Host controls deadlines/concurrency/output budgets independently of caller."
  ],
  "evidence_notes": [
    "Contract source only; not an implementation or runtime qualification.",
    "Current installed Codex metadata/login probe is presence/auth evidence only. Actual model, configured permissions enforcement and cancel/drain behavior remain unverified until the separately registered real path is observed.",
    "No D source or frozen worktree was edited to produce this contract.",
    "D03 revision2: reuse the native Harness under its existing trusted machine/account policy. Actual Windows readonly boundary/events/cancel remain separately unverified; known policy incompatibility or uncontrolled project inheritance blocks only that Run."
  ]
